Feature: PetStore API CRUD Operations\n  As a user of the PetStore API\n  I want to perform CRUD operations on pets\n  So that I can manage pet data effectively\n\n  Background:\n    Given the API endpoint is \"https://petstore.swagger.io/v2/pet\"\n\n  @create\n  Scenario: Create a new pet\n    When I send a POST request with the following data:\n      | id  | name   | status     |\n      | 101 | Fluffy | available  |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Fluffy\"\n\n  @read\n  Scenario: Retrieve a pet by ID\n    Given the pet ID is 101\n    When I send a GET request\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Fluffy\"\n\n  @update\n  Scenario: Update an existing pet\n    When I send a PUT request with the following data:\n      | id  | name   | status |\n      | 101 | Fluffy | sold   |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"sold\"\n\n  @delete\n  Scenario: Delete a pet by ID\n    Given the pet ID is 101\n    When I send a DELETE request\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: Retrieve a non-existent pet\n    Given the pet ID is 999\n    When I send a GET request\n    Then the response status code should be 404